  "behavior": [
    "Substrate signers explicitly snapshot their payload and existing local/mobile configuration before the queue admission authorization await. Accounts are cloned at the same boundary.",
    "Substrate publishes detached account/payload data only, without execution methods. Solana similarly detaches published account, options, transaction batches and previews from private request state.",
    "Both queues reject duplicate active IDs. Resolver/rejector completion is one-shot and checks captured object ownership, so a retained callback cannot remove a later request that reused the ID.",
    "Solana fee/simulation work uses the captured transaction and updates only its original request object. Delayed results cannot attach to a later owner with the same ID."
  ],
